WEBVTT

1
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:42.751
Come on, Gus-Gus. Faster!

2
00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:46.004
What's the hurry, Jaq-Jaq?
What's the hurry?

3
00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:47.505
Fairy Godmother's here.

4
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.050
She's gonna read us
the Cinderelly story.

5
00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:52.594
Pom-Pom.

6
00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:24.459
Come on, Gus!

7
00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:31.549
"Cinderella and the Prince
lived happily ever after.

8
00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:35.095
"The end."

9
00:01:36.681 --> 00:01:37.889
We missed it?

10
00:01:39.475 --> 00:01:43.019
-Maybe you could read another one.
-I'm sorry, Gus,

11
00:01:43.104 --> 00:01:45.981
but that's the only
Cinderella book there is.

12
00:01:46.065 --> 00:01:50.819
Yeah, Gus-Gus. You heard her.
The end. That's all.

13
00:01:50.903 --> 00:01:53.446
Maybe we could make another book.

14
00:01:53.531 --> 00:01:56.324
-We can tell the stories.
-And make the drawings!

15
00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:57.701
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

16
00:01:57.785 --> 00:02:00.662
What an excellent idea.

17
00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:02.664
No, no, wait a minute.

18
00:02:02.748 --> 00:02:05.375
Who'd wanna read a book
made by mice?

19
00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:07.544
Cinderella would read it.

20
00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:11.548
And if you made it,
I know that she'd love it.

21
00:02:11.632 --> 00:02:13.800
But we don't know how to make a book.

22
00:02:13.884 --> 00:02:17.721
Don't worry, dear. I think I can help.

23
00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:25.437
Salagadoola mechicka boola
ibbbbdb-bobbbdb-boo

24
00:02:25.521 --> 00:02:27.731
Put 'em together
and what have you got?

25
00:02:27.815 --> 00:02:29.357
ibbbbdb-bobbbdb-boo

26
00:02:44.874 --> 00:02:46.124
Now, what do we need?

27
00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.542
-A pencil, indeed.
-And crayons.

28
00:02:47.626 --> 00:02:48.918
-And glitter.
-And glue.

29
00:02:49.003 --> 00:02:51.338
We'll sew up the book
with a thread and a hook.

30
00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:53.173
ibbbbdb-bobbbdb-boo

31
00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:57.844
Very nice. Well done, little mice.
But something is missing, it's true.

32
00:02:57.928 --> 00:03:00.055
Look there. The pages are bare.

33
00:03:00.139 --> 00:03:03.600
-We need a story from you.
-Who, us?

34
00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:06.227
No, no, we don't know any good stories.

35
00:03:06.312 --> 00:03:10.815
Wait, wait!
How's about "First Day in Castle"?

36
00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.902
Oh, yeah. That is a good one.

37
00:03:14.653 --> 00:03:17.614
I'd love to hear all about it.

38
00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:28.750
It was right after
Cinderelly and the Prince married.

39
00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.669
Mice-mice moved to the big castIe.

40
00:03:31.754 --> 00:03:33.797
We had it all to ourselves,

41
00:03:33.881 --> 00:03:37.050
and we were having
the time of our lives.

42
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.810
Cinderelly's back!

43
00:03:46.894 --> 00:03:49.646
-Oh, dear, they're back!
-They're back!

44
00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:54.442
-They're back!
-They're back!

45
00:04:02.785 --> 00:04:05.703
-We're back!
-Welcome home.

46
00:04:05.788 --> 00:04:08.623
I still can't believe
I'm going to live in a castle.

47
00:04:08.707 --> 00:04:11.292
Are you sure this isn't just a dream?

48
00:04:11.377 --> 00:04:13.211
You're a princess now.

49
00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:16.881
Princess Cinderella.

50
00:04:16.966 --> 00:04:20.260
She won't even know the first thing
about being a princess.

51
00:04:20.344 --> 00:04:23.346
She just got back from her honeymoon.

52
00:04:23.431 --> 00:04:26.349
It's going to be your duty
to prepare the girl.

53
00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:29.269
Your Majesty, I am honoured.

54
00:04:29.353 --> 00:04:32.021
Not you, ninny. Prudence!

55
00:04:32.106 --> 00:04:33.565
Of course not you.

56
00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:37.110
He wants the job done right
the first time.

57
00:04:37.194 --> 00:04:41.573
The royal banquet
will be Cinderella's responsibility now.

58
00:04:41.657 --> 00:04:44.075
The royal banquet?

59
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.786
You'll teach her everything
she needs to know.

60
00:04:46.871 --> 00:04:51.958
But, sire, she won't know anything
about planning a royal banquet.

61
00:04:52.042 --> 00:04:55.170
I don't know anything about
planning a royal banquet.

62
00:04:55.254 --> 00:04:57.547
Oh, well.
At least I can stay past midnight.

63
00:04:58.174 --> 00:05:01.050
Perfect! And I'll be right by your side.

64
00:05:01.427 --> 00:05:03.761
I have to go? Now?

65
00:05:04.388 --> 00:05:06.973
Father, I can't just
abandon my princess!

66
00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:09.934
Not with the royal banquet
only two days away.

67
00:05:10.019 --> 00:05:13.730
Nonsense! We have important
matters of state to attend to.

68
00:05:13.814 --> 00:05:16.065
Important matters of state!

69
00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.984
Father...

70
00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:20.195
She hasn't had time to prepare.

71
00:05:20.279 --> 00:05:22.405
She's never been a princess before.

72
00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:28.036
I dare say, Majesty,
you do like your banquets just so, eh?

73
00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.955
It's a great deal to ask of the poor girl.

74
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.457
Nonsense!

75
00:05:32.541 --> 00:05:37.962
Your Majesty, I can take care
of the preparations as I always do.

76
00:05:38.047 --> 00:05:40.548
Just show her what to do!

77
00:05:40.633 --> 00:05:45.053
We have a princess now.
It's her duty to plan the banquet.

78
00:05:45.137 --> 00:05:49.390
And the King's duty to endure it.

79
00:05:50.226 --> 00:05:52.143
Yes, Your Majesty.

80
00:05:52.228 --> 00:05:55.230
Now off we go!

81
00:05:55.731 --> 00:05:58.650
-Thank you.
-I'm sorry I have to rush off.

82
00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:00.860
Don't worry. I'll be fine.

83
00:06:00.945 --> 00:06:04.322
I know you're gonna surprise us
with an incredible feast.

84
00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:06.991
I just hope you're not too surprised.

85
00:06:37.106 --> 00:06:39.440
Cinderelly!

86
00:06:40.776 --> 00:06:44.904
Jaq! Gus! Mary! Hello, old friends.

87
00:06:46.615 --> 00:06:47.949
Bruno!

88
00:06:49.285 --> 00:06:53.621
Look-look.
Big chair for Princess Cinderelly!

89
00:06:55.624 --> 00:06:56.916
Oh, my.

90
00:06:59.795 --> 00:07:01.921
Big castle, too.

91
00:07:02.006 --> 00:07:06.217
Don't worry, Cinderelly.
Us mice here to help.

92
00:07:06.302 --> 00:07:10.221
Why, thank you, Jaq. We've got
a big day ahead of us tomorrow.

93
00:07:15.269 --> 00:07:16.644
This way, fellas.

94
00:07:38.459 --> 00:07:40.585
Good morning, Your Highness.

95
00:07:43.339 --> 00:07:44.714
Your Highness!

96
00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:53.348
Ready for breakfast?
How does a cheese omelette sound?

97
00:07:54.475 --> 00:07:56.517
The Princess is missing!

98
00:07:58.312 --> 00:08:01.898
You! You, girl!
Have you seen the Princess?

99
00:08:01.982 --> 00:08:03.941
Good morning, Prudence.

100
00:08:04.026 --> 00:08:08.988
Oh, I thought you...
But those awful clothes!

101
00:08:09.073 --> 00:08:13.242
Well, I didn't recognise you,
Your Highness.

102
00:08:13.327 --> 00:08:15.995
Allow me to introduce
your ladies-in-waiting.

103
00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.332
-Beatrice and Daphne.
-Pleased to meet you.

104
00:08:19.416 --> 00:08:21.417
You're just in time for breakfast.

105
00:08:21.502 --> 00:08:24.962
Breakfast? With toast and jam?

106
00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:31.260
Your Highness, a princess
never prepares her own meals.

107
00:08:31.345 --> 00:08:35.139
That is not how things are done.

108
00:08:35.224 --> 00:08:37.350
There are rules about breakfast?

109
00:08:37.434 --> 00:08:40.812
Of course there are rules,
Your Highness.

110
00:08:40.896 --> 00:08:45.358
But it's not your fault that you
don't know the traditions of the castle.

111
00:08:45.442 --> 00:08:49.237
That's what the King
expects me to teach you.

112
00:08:49.363 --> 00:08:51.906
I'm sure I can learn it in no time.

113
00:08:53.075 --> 00:08:54.659
Come along.
There's no time to dally.

114
00:08:54.743 --> 00:08:57.912
Just do as I say,
and everything will be fine.

115
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.335
The King would be horrified

116
00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:09.590
to find the hostess of the royal banquet
dressed like a scullery maid!

117
00:09:09.675 --> 00:09:13.136
A princess must be attired like royalty.

118
00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.181
Do I have to wear this all the time?

119
00:09:17.266 --> 00:09:19.434
Oh, of course not, Your Highness.

120
00:09:19.518 --> 00:09:22.103
You'll need something
much more formal for dinner.

121
00:09:23.272 --> 00:09:25.940
Couldn't I just wear
one of my own dresses?

122
00:09:27.651 --> 00:09:32.113
Very amusing, Your Highness,
but it simply isn't done.

123
00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:47.920
It's such a beautiful day.
Why don't we open the curtains?

124
00:09:48.005 --> 00:09:51.507
No, no, no!
These curtains are never opened.

125
00:09:52.801 --> 00:09:55.970
And certainly not by a princess.

126
00:09:56.054 --> 00:09:59.307
It most definitely isn't done.

127
00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:05.271
Dukes and viscounts
sit nearest the King

128
00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:07.482
unless there is a marquis present.

129
00:10:07.566 --> 00:10:10.568
Wouldn't it be nice
if people could sit where they like?

130
00:10:10.652 --> 00:10:16.491
No. You must never seat a duke
above a marquis or below a baron.

131
00:10:16.992 --> 00:10:19.577
Which colour is correct, Your Highness?

132
00:10:19.661 --> 00:10:21.954
Cream or ecru?

133
00:10:22.873 --> 00:10:24.248
Ecru?

134
00:10:24.333 --> 00:10:26.626
Goodness, no. Cream.

135
00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:28.711
But there isn't any difference.

136
00:10:28.796 --> 00:10:32.799
Oh, my. So much to learn. So little time.

137
00:10:34.635 --> 00:10:37.762
At the banquet, as always,

138
00:10:37.846 --> 00:10:41.224
the royal menu shall consist
of the rarest roast beef,

139
00:10:41.308 --> 00:10:45.186
French onion soup, tarragon mashed
potatoes, freshly baked baguettes,

140
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:49.357
the finest truffles in the kingdom
and, for dessert,

141
00:10:50.025 --> 00:10:52.568
Norwegian stewed prunes.

142
00:10:53.111 --> 00:10:56.239
Prunes? For dessert?

143
00:10:56.323 --> 00:11:00.284
The King expects it.
It is a tradition that is never broken.

144
00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:03.371
Besides, I like them.

145
00:11:07.543 --> 00:11:11.587
Your Highness shall pause here
to greet her noble guests.

146
00:11:11.672 --> 00:11:15.800
Remember.
Curtsy to royalty, wave to nobility.

147
00:11:15.884 --> 00:11:18.594
I know I can do this right.

148
00:11:18.679 --> 00:11:21.389
-Cinderella!
-Cinderella! Hi!

149
00:11:21.473 --> 00:11:24.642
My friends! Hello! Hello!

150
00:11:24.726 --> 00:11:28.563
How nice to see you. Wait just a minute.

151
00:11:28.647 --> 00:11:31.482
-Open the gate!
-No, no, no!

152
00:11:31.567 --> 00:11:34.694
These gates are only opened
for royal visitors.

153
00:11:36.154 --> 00:11:39.407
You must remember the rules.

154
00:11:40.158 --> 00:11:43.244
Commoners are never allowed
in the palace.

155
00:11:43.328 --> 00:11:45.121
It simply isn't done.

156
00:11:47.791 --> 00:11:49.584
Bye-bye!

157
00:12:15.569 --> 00:12:18.779
At the very least,
one must learn to dance

158
00:12:18.864 --> 00:12:21.073
with poise and grace.

159
00:12:21.158 --> 00:12:25.536
I'm trying, I just need more practise.

160
00:12:27.122 --> 00:12:31.876
It must be perfect.
It is the King's favourite dance.

161
00:12:38.467 --> 00:12:43.346
No, no, no, Your Highness.
It must be slower and more formal.

162
00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.015
Your Highness, eggshell or bone?

163
00:12:46.099 --> 00:12:47.725
-Eggshell?
-Bone.

164
00:12:47.809 --> 00:12:50.394
Now, who sits next to the count?

165
00:12:50.479 --> 00:12:52.772
-The duke?
-The marquis.

166
00:12:52.856 --> 00:12:54.607
-Gold or silver?
-For what?

167
00:12:54.691 --> 00:12:57.151
-Baron or viscount?
-Who?

168
00:12:57.235 --> 00:12:59.779
-Pekoe or Darjeeling?
-I don't know!

169
00:12:59.863 --> 00:13:01.572
Braised or broiled?

170
00:13:01.657 --> 00:13:03.574
-Fish or fowl?
-Stand or sit?

171
00:13:03.659 --> 00:13:05.743
-Mind the music!
-Hair up or down?

172
00:13:05.827 --> 00:13:07.328
-Left or right?
-One or two?

173
00:13:07.412 --> 00:13:09.372
-Watch the chair!
-Your Highness!

174
00:13:17.381 --> 00:13:22.176
Your Highness, the dance
is best performed on one's feet.

175
00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:44.198
This is a disaster.

176
00:14:01.675 --> 00:14:04.510
Poor Cinderelly. Please don't cry.

177
00:14:04.594 --> 00:14:08.889
Cinderelly not happy,
mice-mice not happy.

178
00:14:08.974 --> 00:14:12.184
Jaq, what am I going to do?

179
00:14:12.269 --> 00:14:15.396
I'm a complete failure as a princess.

180
00:14:19.735 --> 00:14:22.236
Why can't I learn to do this right?

181
00:14:25.782 --> 00:14:27.450
Look at me.

182
00:14:27.534 --> 00:14:29.702
Cinderelly not look like Cinderelly.

183
00:14:29.786 --> 00:14:34.373
It's true. Something's just not right here.

184
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.585
Like stewed prunes?

185
00:14:37.669 --> 00:14:42.173
Exactly, Gus. And why do they
have to keep the palace so dark?

186
00:14:42.257 --> 00:14:44.341
And that awful dance.

187
00:14:44.426 --> 00:14:47.303
And those boring colours
that all look the same.

188
00:14:47.387 --> 00:14:48.763
And stewed prunes!

189
00:14:48.847 --> 00:14:52.600
Especially those rules about
keeping commoners out of the palace!

190
00:14:52.684 --> 00:14:55.352
Why, I was a dish maid
when the Prince married me.

191
00:14:55.437 --> 00:14:58.606
And he loves me because I'm me.

192
00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:03.027
I've been trying to obey someone else's
rules about who I should be

193
00:15:03.111 --> 00:15:05.029
and how I should dress.

194
00:15:08.450 --> 00:15:09.825
This hair!

195
00:15:12.204 --> 00:15:16.123
I know I can do this. I just have to
stop trying to be someone else.

196
00:15:16.917 --> 00:15:18.542
What'll she do, Jaq-Jaq?

197
00:15:18.627 --> 00:15:22.922
Gus, I'm going to plan
this banquet my way.

198
00:15:23.715 --> 00:15:27.968
Who's to say the ruIes
must stay the same forevermore?

199
00:15:28.053 --> 00:15:30.221
Open the gates!

200
00:15:30.305 --> 00:15:36.936
Whoever made them had to change
the rules that came before

201
00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:39.230
So make your own way

202
00:15:39.314 --> 00:15:42.274
Show the beauty within

203
00:15:42.359 --> 00:15:48.322
When you foIIow your heart
there's no heart you can't win

204
00:15:49.491 --> 00:15:51.826
Why, thank you!

205
00:15:54.496 --> 00:15:57.289
Your Highness,
the King would not approve.

206
00:15:57.374 --> 00:16:01.127
You're supposed to be inviting dukes
and counts and other aristocrats.

207
00:16:01.211 --> 00:16:05.506
I am inviting them, along with
all my friends here in the village.

208
00:16:06.049 --> 00:16:10.427
Your Highness,
I strongly advise against it.

209
00:16:10.512 --> 00:16:14.473
It's simply not the way things are done.

210
00:16:15.392 --> 00:16:19.228
Perhaps the time has come
to try something new.

211
00:16:19.312 --> 00:16:23.732
So reach for the sky
it's not high as it seems

212
00:16:23.817 --> 00:16:30.072
Just foIIow your heart
go as far as your dreams

213
00:16:30.157 --> 00:16:34.201
This party needs help,
starting with dessert.

214
00:16:34.286 --> 00:16:36.495
No prunes. Yuck!

215
00:16:37.247 --> 00:16:39.957
Jaq-Jaq love chocolate.

216
00:16:46.506 --> 00:16:50.718
Chocolate pudding!
Now that sounds good.

217
00:17:01.813 --> 00:17:04.148
We never get to dance like this.

218
00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:09.904
Dance if you want to
don't fear you'II faII

219
00:17:14.075 --> 00:17:20.915
Take a chance, 'cause it's better
than never to chance it at all

220
00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:26.629
It simply isn't done. It simply isn't done!

221
00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:31.675
It simply isn't done!

222
00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:37.264
It simply isn't done,
it simply isn't done, it simply isn't done.

223
00:17:39.935 --> 00:17:43.979
There's a world fuII of changing
and you've just begun

224
00:17:44.105 --> 00:17:47.650
Don't Iet them teII you
it's simpIy not done

225
00:17:47.734 --> 00:17:54.657
When you foIIow your heart
you'II shine bright as the sun

226
00:17:56.868 --> 00:18:01.413
-Your Highness, sand or buff?
-Which colour do you like?

227
00:18:02.582 --> 00:18:03.624
Pink!

228
00:18:04.626 --> 00:18:05.918
Perfect.

229
00:18:07.879 --> 00:18:11.048
Something's still missing.

230
00:18:14.469 --> 00:18:16.428
Now, that's more like it.

231
00:18:18.974 --> 00:18:22.518
-What will the King say?
-I know this is a big change.

232
00:18:22.602 --> 00:18:24.561
But I have to try this my way.

233
00:18:25.313 --> 00:18:30.609
Well, then, I certainly hope
you know what you're doing.

234
00:18:38.827 --> 00:18:41.495
They're here, Cinderelly! They're here!

235
00:18:45.417 --> 00:18:48.168
Well, it's too late to turn back now.

236
00:19:06.438 --> 00:19:08.772
Now, this dance is more like it.

237
00:19:16.656 --> 00:19:19.533
This dance is horrifying!

238
00:19:44.976 --> 00:19:47.561
The King has arrived.

239
00:19:54.444 --> 00:19:56.070
Pudding!

240
00:20:00.742 --> 00:20:03.660
What in blazes is going on here?

241
00:20:03.745 --> 00:20:05.204
Your Majesty!

242
00:20:07.332 --> 00:20:11.543
-Who opened those curtains?
-This is all Princess Cinderella's doing!

243
00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:14.880
What a lovely moon.

244
00:20:14.964 --> 00:20:19.343
-I tried to teach her, sire.
-Commoners in the palace?

245
00:20:19.427 --> 00:20:21.804
She simply refused to listen.

246
00:20:21.888 --> 00:20:25.557
-Oh, hello, Giuseppe!
-It's a scandal!

247
00:20:25.642 --> 00:20:28.352
Your Majesty, I can explain.

248
00:20:28.436 --> 00:20:30.479
What is this?

249
00:20:30.563 --> 00:20:32.481
Your dessert, sire.

250
00:20:33.191 --> 00:20:35.984
No prunes for dessert?

251
00:20:36.069 --> 00:20:38.362
An absolute outrage!

252
00:20:40.615 --> 00:20:42.866
Chocolate. My favourite!

253
00:20:46.955 --> 00:20:51.041
What happened to the music?
Everybody dance!

254
00:21:07.809 --> 00:21:11.019
I always said we needed
some new traditions around here.

255
00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:15.149
Go on, now, Prudence.
You're missing all the fun.

256
00:21:25.368 --> 00:21:27.744
-Did I miss something?
-Surprise!

257
00:21:29.622 --> 00:21:31.915
Splendid job. Splendid!

258
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:36.170
It is the Princess
who deserves your praise, sire.

259
00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:41.216
And I am honoured to be
at Her Highness's service.

260
00:21:41.301 --> 00:21:44.178
I think we're going to be great friends.

261
00:22:03.323 --> 00:22:06.450
I told my son he had chosen well.

262
00:22:06.534 --> 00:22:08.911
You're a natural.

263
00:22:08.995 --> 00:22:12.331
Hooray! Hooray!

264
00:22:12.415 --> 00:22:14.124
Another dance!

265
00:22:15.084 --> 00:22:17.461
I'm glad you do things your own way.

266
00:22:17.545 --> 00:22:20.130
Someday I'll get
this princess thing right.

267
00:22:20.215 --> 00:22:22.257
I think that day is today.

268
00:22:31.226 --> 00:22:35.979
Well, Cinderella certainly
turned things around, didn't she?

269
00:22:36.064 --> 00:22:38.148
Yeah, no more big hair.

270
00:22:38.233 --> 00:22:39.900
Or prunes.

271
00:22:48.243 --> 00:22:50.077
Can't get it.

272
00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:53.205
Let me help with that.

273
00:22:56.376 --> 00:22:59.044
Watch it. I don't like that magic stuff.

274
00:22:59.128 --> 00:23:04.383
-Remember what happened last time.
-Oh, now there's a story we should tell.

275
00:23:04.467 --> 00:23:06.718
Yeah, that's a good one!

276
00:23:08.721 --> 00:23:12.182
Oh, no. No, no, no.
Very, very boring story.

277
00:23:12.267 --> 00:23:14.518
We don't want to hear that one.

278
00:23:14.602 --> 00:23:18.689
-But, Jaq, it's my favourite.
-Okay, let's hear it.

279
00:23:18.773 --> 00:23:22.693
Well, it certainly was
an unusual wish, Jaq, dear.

280
00:23:22.777 --> 00:23:27.364
iut things didn't turn out
quite the way you had pIanned.

281
00:23:27.448 --> 00:23:30.867
What are we doing
in the garden, Jaq-Jaq?

282
00:23:30.952 --> 00:23:33.161
Gus-Gus not had breakfast yet.

283
00:23:34.414 --> 00:23:37.374
Gus-Gus, we're going to pick flowers
for Cinderelly.

284
00:23:37.458 --> 00:23:38.875
What for?

285
00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:41.378
We never get to do anything
for Cinderelly now.

286
00:23:41.462 --> 00:23:43.505
Sure we do.

287
00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:47.342
-Like what?
-Well, let's see.

288
00:23:47.427 --> 00:23:48.927
See?

289
00:23:50.179 --> 00:23:54.891
Cinderelly don't need mice-mice.
She got lots of people to help her.

290
00:23:54.976 --> 00:23:58.145
Well, I want to bring her
a big bunch of flowers.

291
00:24:21.836 --> 00:24:25.380
-That's enough!
-You've got to think big, Gus-Gus.

292
00:24:27.508 --> 00:24:28.842
Pom-Pom!

293
00:24:53.451 --> 00:24:56.453
-Your flowers, Highness.
-Well, thank you.

294
00:24:56.537 --> 00:25:00.374
Oh, these are even prettier
than yesterday's.

295
00:25:00.875 --> 00:25:05.212
Here's the list of remaining preparations
for the festival tomorrow.

296
00:25:07.006 --> 00:25:10.050
We sure throw a lot of parties
around here, don't we?

297
00:25:10.134 --> 00:25:12.469
This is no mere party, Highness.

298
00:25:12.553 --> 00:25:15.097
This is the Spring Festival!

299
00:25:21.229 --> 00:25:24.481
Oh, good morning, fellas.
What do you have there?

300
00:25:25.024 --> 00:25:28.110
For you. But they're too small.

301
00:25:30.738 --> 00:25:34.991
They're beautiful!
How very sweet. Thank you.

302
00:25:35.785 --> 00:25:37.619
Your Highness, the festival committee

303
00:25:37.704 --> 00:25:39.287
is assembled in the library

304
00:25:39.372 --> 00:25:41.873
awaiting your instructions.

305
00:25:41.958 --> 00:25:45.877
And the bath is in the pantry
awaiting you.

306
00:25:45.962 --> 00:25:47.754
I'll see you later, boys.

307
00:25:49.090 --> 00:25:50.590
Good morning, Jaq.

308
00:25:51.259 --> 00:25:53.969
Hello, Mary. Pretty coat!

309
00:25:54.762 --> 00:25:56.430
I made it for you.

310
00:25:58.725 --> 00:26:00.726
Want to try it on?

311
00:26:00.810 --> 00:26:03.103
Oh, very nice.

312
00:26:03.771 --> 00:26:05.814
Cinderelly forgot party list!

313
00:26:07.775 --> 00:26:10.444
Jaq can help. Take list to Cinderelly!

314
00:26:18.619 --> 00:26:22.247
I got it! No problem.

315
00:26:23.291 --> 00:26:24.583
I'll be right back.

316
00:26:28.337 --> 00:26:32.007
The Prince and I will
cut the ribbon to begin the festival.

317
00:26:32.091 --> 00:26:33.592
Any other suggestions?

318
00:26:33.676 --> 00:26:38.096
I propose we move
the Spring Festival to summer.

319
00:26:38.181 --> 00:26:42.225
Genius!
I wish I had thought of it myself.

320
00:26:42.310 --> 00:26:45.729
It wouldn't be
a Spring Festival any more.

321
00:26:45.813 --> 00:26:47.147
Yes, yes, quite so.

322
00:26:47.231 --> 00:26:49.941
Of course not,
I dare say, Your Highness.

323
00:26:50.026 --> 00:26:51.067
Yummy.

324
00:26:51.152 --> 00:26:54.237
Perhaps we should
not invite the children.

325
00:26:54.322 --> 00:26:59.075
-Can't open.
-No children. A brilliant idea.

326
00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:01.203
The festival is for children.

327
00:27:01.287 --> 00:27:03.789
An even more brilliant rebuttal!

328
00:27:03.873 --> 00:27:08.752
Oh, I suppose.
But the lines are so long.

329
00:27:08.836 --> 00:27:11.755
No problem.
We'll add more rides.

330
00:27:16.677 --> 00:27:21.389
Help! I can't stand mice!
Oh, no! Disgusting!

331
00:27:33.069 --> 00:27:35.111
Jaq, are you all right?

332
00:27:35.196 --> 00:27:39.324
No help to Cinderelly.
Just make a big mess.

333
00:27:39.408 --> 00:27:42.285
I'm sorry, Jaq. Tell you what.

334
00:27:42.370 --> 00:27:45.789
I'm about to go out to the fairgrounds.
Why don't you come?

335
00:27:45.873 --> 00:27:49.668
-I could really use your help.
-Help? Zug-zug!

336
00:27:49.752 --> 00:27:52.462
Meet me at the stables in ten minutes.

337
00:27:52.547 --> 00:27:53.880
No problem.

338
00:27:55.883 --> 00:27:57.717
Here we are. There, Charger.

339
00:28:13.234 --> 00:28:17.237
Wow. Not sure Cinderelly
can find me down here.

340
00:28:31.377 --> 00:28:32.586
Jaq?

341
00:28:34.088 --> 00:28:36.923
-Jaq?
-Hey, Cind...

342
00:28:40.511 --> 00:28:41.553
Jaq?

343
00:28:41.637 --> 00:28:44.639
Your Highness,
your escort is waiting outside.

344
00:28:44.724 --> 00:28:46.933
Thank you. Jaq?

345
00:28:47.310 --> 00:28:48.518
Cinderelly!

346
00:28:49.437 --> 00:28:51.938
Oh, well. I guess he couldn't come.

347
00:28:53.065 --> 00:28:54.274
Oh, no!

348
00:28:56.611 --> 00:28:58.778
Cinderelly, wait!

349
00:29:10.499 --> 00:29:12.125
Cinderelly!

350
00:29:14.795 --> 00:29:17.005
Hey!

351
00:29:17.632 --> 00:29:19.132
Hey.

352
00:29:27.016 --> 00:29:28.391
Cinderelly?

353
00:29:30.937 --> 00:29:35.065
I never get to do anything any more.
I never get to help.

354
00:29:35.149 --> 00:29:38.109
Get left behind sitting in the dirt.
Used to help a lot.

355
00:29:38.194 --> 00:29:41.613
Now I'm too small to do this,
too small to do that,

356
00:29:41.697 --> 00:29:43.657
too small to help Cinderelly.

357
00:29:43.741 --> 00:29:45.325
No good to anybody!

358
00:29:46.327 --> 00:29:47.577
Castle not like old house.

359
00:29:47.662 --> 00:29:50.455
Castle for big people.
No place for mice!

360
00:29:50.539 --> 00:29:53.500
Everything's bigger than me.
Even flowers bigger!

361
00:29:54.168 --> 00:29:57.003
Don't like being small.
Don't like being a mouse.

362
00:29:57.088 --> 00:29:58.463
I wish I was big!

363
00:30:12.520 --> 00:30:14.145
There, there, dear.

364
00:30:14.981 --> 00:30:17.065
Tell me all...

365
00:30:17.149 --> 00:30:19.150
Jaq? Jaq?

366
00:30:21.946 --> 00:30:24.572
Oh, there you are, dear.

367
00:30:25.533 --> 00:30:29.911
I heard your wish, Jaq.
Aren't you happy the way you are?

368
00:30:29.996 --> 00:30:33.039
Only big people help Cinderelly.
I want to be big!

369
00:30:33.124 --> 00:30:35.792
No, I want to be human.

370
00:30:35.876 --> 00:30:38.128
Human? Oh, good heavens!

371
00:30:38.212 --> 00:30:43.550
But, Jaq, you've always helped
Cinderella just the way you are.

372
00:30:43.634 --> 00:30:47.345
Cinderelly's a princess now.
No time for mice.

373
00:30:47.430 --> 00:30:49.097
Nobody likes mice anyway.

374
00:30:49.181 --> 00:30:51.182
So that's what you think.

375
00:30:51.892 --> 00:30:56.604
I get beat up by cat and horse
and big, scary lady!

376
00:30:58.691 --> 00:31:01.401
Humans are bigger. Bigger better.

377
00:31:02.069 --> 00:31:05.071
If you really feel that way

378
00:31:06.532 --> 00:31:10.910
perhaps it would be for the best
to grant your wish.

379
00:31:12.872 --> 00:31:15.582
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo!

380
00:31:27.261 --> 00:31:30.972
The sun's up shining, siIver Iining

381
00:31:31.057 --> 00:31:33.183
It's gonna be a beautifuI day

382
00:31:33.267 --> 00:31:36.811
Jaq. The human Jaq. How do you do?

383
00:31:36.896 --> 00:31:40.648
Church bells ringing, birds all singing

384
00:31:40.733 --> 00:31:43.443
Everything's going my way

385
00:31:43.527 --> 00:31:46.529
Zug-zug. I really am human.

386
00:31:48.449 --> 00:31:52.035
Climb the trees, smell the breeze

387
00:31:52.119 --> 00:31:55.789
Laugh with aII your might

388
00:31:55.873 --> 00:32:01.461
iIue skies showing
everything's going right

389
00:32:03.631 --> 00:32:06.966
You'II never stop the raining
by sitting and compIaining

390
00:32:07.051 --> 00:32:11.054
It aII comes down to you

391
00:32:11.138 --> 00:32:14.724
You'II smiIe again, it happens when

392
00:32:14.809 --> 00:32:17.227
You change your point of view

393
00:32:17.311 --> 00:32:21.231
I love the view from up here!

394
00:32:21.315 --> 00:32:24.234
When you're smaII, one-inch taII

395
00:32:24.318 --> 00:32:27.904
And then you're 6'2"

396
00:32:27.988 --> 00:32:33.451
You've hit the big time now
and the world is Iooking up to you

397
00:32:33.536 --> 00:32:35.995
There she is. What am I going to say?

398
00:32:37.540 --> 00:32:40.166
Princess Cinderelly, it's me, Jaq!

399
00:32:40.251 --> 00:32:43.628
Look, I'm human now.
I'm human now, too!

400
00:32:43.712 --> 00:32:47.382
When you're smaII, one-inch taII

401
00:32:47.466 --> 00:32:50.760
And then you're 6'2"

402
00:32:50.845 --> 00:32:52.637
You've hit the big time now

403
00:32:52.721 --> 00:32:54.013
Cinderelly! It's me!

404
00:32:54.098 --> 00:32:56.266
The world is Iooking up to you

405
00:32:56.350 --> 00:32:57.892
Yeah, you

406
00:32:57.977 --> 00:33:00.061
-My dear sir.
-Oh, you poor man!

407
00:33:00.146 --> 00:33:01.938
-Sir...
-I'm...

408
00:33:02.022 --> 00:33:03.857
Sir Hugh, is it?

409
00:33:03.941 --> 00:33:08.278
-Well, then. Pleased to know you.
-I knows to please you, too!

410
00:33:08.362 --> 00:33:10.989
-Are you all right, Sir Hugh?
-Yes, yes, I...

411
00:33:11.073 --> 00:33:14.701
-Hugh, eh? Would that be Belgian?
-What? Eh, no, no.

412
00:33:14.785 --> 00:33:16.870
No, no, no, of course not. No accent.

413
00:33:16.954 --> 00:33:20.790
I'm so sorry about the mess.
Here, let me help you.

414
00:33:20.875 --> 00:33:24.127
No, no, that's why I'm here.
To help you. I'm...

415
00:33:24.211 --> 00:33:26.254
The committee sent you!

416
00:33:26.338 --> 00:33:28.965
You're here to help
with the Spring Festival?

417
00:33:29.049 --> 00:33:31.968
-You're Dutch!
-No. I mean yes. But I'm...

418
00:33:33.470 --> 00:33:37.390
Late! Your Highness, it is late.
We're expected back at the palace.

419
00:33:37.474 --> 00:33:42.145
-Shall we ride back together?
-Ride? On horses?

420
00:33:43.314 --> 00:33:45.565
-Nice horsie!
-Sir Hugh?

421
00:33:47.401 --> 00:33:48.985
Have you ridden before?

422
00:33:51.572 --> 00:33:55.783
Sir Hugh? Sir Hugh? There you are.

423
00:33:58.329 --> 00:34:00.830
Peach blossoms.

424
00:34:00.915 --> 00:34:03.750
Aren't you sweet?
They're beautiful. Thank you.

425
00:34:06.921 --> 00:34:08.963
Highness, there you are.

426
00:34:09.048 --> 00:34:11.841
The tailor is in a dither.
The cook is having a crisis.

427
00:34:11.926 --> 00:34:15.678
The animal trainer is flummoxed!
And they're all asking for you.

428
00:34:15.763 --> 00:34:19.766
Could you please find a vase for these?
I'll be right back.

429
00:34:19.850 --> 00:34:22.352
Thank you, Sir Hugh. You're a big help.

430
00:34:26.774 --> 00:34:30.109
Perfect.
Helping Cinderelly with flowers.

431
00:34:46.752 --> 00:34:48.086
Pom-Pom!

432
00:34:54.134 --> 00:34:55.969
I shouldn't be afraid of cat!

433
00:34:58.931 --> 00:35:01.599
I am human now. Bigger than cat.

434
00:35:02.351 --> 00:35:04.560
But I am still afraid of cat!

435
00:35:11.694 --> 00:35:13.695
Oh, good. You found a vase.

436
00:35:15.656 --> 00:35:18.574
Happy to help. What I want to...

437
00:35:18.659 --> 00:35:21.869
The Countess Legrande
is awaiting you in the dining hall.

438
00:35:21.954 --> 00:35:23.955
Think you could keep
her company till I get there?

439
00:35:30.796 --> 00:35:32.005
A mouse!

440
00:35:35.259 --> 00:35:37.760
What am I doing? I'm a man now.

441
00:35:37.845 --> 00:35:41.723
-A big, fat mouse!
-Oh, no. Gus-Gus!

442
00:35:43.183 --> 00:35:44.434
Get away!

443
00:35:54.028 --> 00:35:57.572
My hero. Oh, you saved me.

444
00:35:57.656 --> 00:36:01.534
Well, I think we just found the couple
to lead the first dance.

445
00:36:04.913 --> 00:36:08.291
We better go get ready.
I'll send a valet for you, Sir Hugh.

446
00:36:08.375 --> 00:36:10.335
See you at the festival.

447
00:36:23.140 --> 00:36:25.808
Hey, Mary, where's Jaq-Jaq?

448
00:36:25.893 --> 00:36:29.896
I don't know, Gus.
I'm worried about him.

449
00:36:29.980 --> 00:36:31.064
Here I am.

450
00:36:33.275 --> 00:36:34.817
Wait!

451
00:36:37.321 --> 00:36:39.572
It's me.

452
00:36:39.656 --> 00:36:42.867
Jaq, is everything all right, dear?

453
00:36:42.951 --> 00:36:46.037
Yes. Great. No problem.

454
00:36:46.747 --> 00:36:50.500
Well, I think you gave your friends
a bit of a fright.

455
00:36:52.920 --> 00:36:56.339
They ran away from me. Even Mary.

456
00:36:56.423 --> 00:36:59.759
Now surely you don't miss
being a mouse.

457
00:36:59.843 --> 00:37:02.512
No, I guess not.

458
00:37:02.596 --> 00:37:04.931
Aren't you happy being human?

459
00:37:05.015 --> 00:37:08.726
Yeah. Sure not as easy as I thought.

460
00:37:11.814 --> 00:37:13.940
But I know I'll get it.

461
00:37:16.235 --> 00:37:19.195
Cinderella is asking for you.

462
00:37:19.279 --> 00:37:21.739
The evening's festivities are upon us.

463
00:37:24.952 --> 00:37:28.287
-Zug-zug!
-Jaq?

464
00:37:28.372 --> 00:37:32.917
Zug-zug, eh? I don't believe
I'm familiar with that expression.

465
00:37:33.001 --> 00:37:36.129
It means... It's French.

466
00:37:36.213 --> 00:37:39.841
French, is it?
Well, that explains everything.

467
00:37:45.097 --> 00:37:48.724
Ladies and gentlemen,
let the Spring Festival begin.

468
00:37:52.938 --> 00:37:56.482
-I'll race you to the Ferris wheel!
-Look there.

469
00:38:02.823 --> 00:38:04.991
Hi, kids!

470
00:38:09.246 --> 00:38:13.124
An elephant! Come on!
I just love elephants!

471
00:38:13.208 --> 00:38:15.877
-Your Majesty...
-Let's go!

472
00:38:16.795 --> 00:38:19.297
Around the world!

473
00:38:19.381 --> 00:38:24.260
Up and down. Up and down.
Around like a Ferris wheel.

474
00:38:24.344 --> 00:38:27.013
Are you sure Jaq-Jaq's here, Mary?

475
00:38:27.097 --> 00:38:29.765
He must be, Gus. Let's find him.

476
00:38:32.895 --> 00:38:35.438
Sir Hugh, are you enjoying yourself?

477
00:38:35.522 --> 00:38:38.608
Well, there's something...

478
00:38:38.692 --> 00:38:42.612
You're not whispering
about me, are you?

479
00:38:42.696 --> 00:38:45.406
I believe I promised you two
the first dance.

480
00:38:52.331 --> 00:38:55.750
What a lovely dancer. Oh, my!

481
00:39:08.222 --> 00:39:09.472
Sir Hugh!

482
00:39:09.556 --> 00:39:11.682
Is that your kitty?

483
00:39:12.809 --> 00:39:14.852
Isn't she precious?

484
00:39:20.317 --> 00:39:22.401
Ready for the next dance?

485
00:39:50.597 --> 00:39:51.764
Nice kitty.

486
00:40:06.989 --> 00:40:09.031
I hate elephants!

487
00:40:16.582 --> 00:40:20.418
This is all my fault!
Wish Fairy Godmother was here.

488
00:40:23.380 --> 00:40:26.048
Jaq, this is your chance to help.

489
00:40:26.133 --> 00:40:27.717
What can I do?

490
00:40:28.468 --> 00:40:32.597
An elephant.
What do you think could stop him?

491
00:40:33.181 --> 00:40:35.558
-Stop in the name of the King!
-Don't know.

492
00:40:35.642 --> 00:40:38.185
Perhaps a mouse?

493
00:40:39.813 --> 00:40:42.898
Aren't all elephants afraid of mice?

494
00:40:44.651 --> 00:40:47.778
Are you a man or a mouse?

495
00:40:52.534 --> 00:40:54.994
I'm a mouse!

496
00:41:01.501 --> 00:41:02.585
Oh, dear, now!

497
00:41:04.588 --> 00:41:06.255
How does it go again?

498
00:41:10.010 --> 00:41:11.552
Oh, yes!

499
00:41:12.095 --> 00:41:14.221
Bibbidi-bobbidi-boo!

500
00:41:18.018 --> 00:41:19.310
Help!

501
00:41:23.398 --> 00:41:26.484
I can see my castle!

502
00:41:34.076 --> 00:41:37.328
I guess there are some things
only a mouse can do.

503
00:41:37.871 --> 00:41:39.330
I'm a mouse!

504
00:41:41.750 --> 00:41:43.209
Yes! I'm a mouse!

505
00:41:44.920 --> 00:41:47.088
I'm a mouse! I'm so glad I'm a mouse!

506
00:41:47.172 --> 00:41:50.675
I'm a mouse! Jaq is back!
I'm a mouse! A mouse!

507
00:41:50.759 --> 00:41:53.511
M-O-U-S-E. I'm a mousie mousie!

508
00:41:53.595 --> 00:41:57.181
Sir Hugh's kitty!

509
00:41:58.392 --> 00:42:02.645
Come, sweetums.
Let's go find your master.

510
00:42:02.729 --> 00:42:06.857
Aren't you just the sweetest,
little, most precious baby?

511
00:42:10.070 --> 00:42:12.822
Jaq, that was so brave!

512
00:42:12.906 --> 00:42:15.408
Mary, I really missed you.

513
00:42:15.492 --> 00:42:17.493
You're a hero!

514
00:42:17.577 --> 00:42:21.747
Jaq, you saved the day!
I can always count on you.

515
00:42:21.832 --> 00:42:24.166
-You're right there when I need you.
-I am?

516
00:42:24.251 --> 00:42:26.252
Yes, you are.

517
00:42:28.547 --> 00:42:30.214
I'm so glad you're back!

518
00:42:33.593 --> 00:42:34.927
Me, too!

519
00:42:56.616 --> 00:43:00.119
-Thank goodness that's over.
-Yeah.

520
00:43:00.203 --> 00:43:03.080
No more magic for Jaq-Jaq!

521
00:43:03.165 --> 00:43:05.541
-Not even a little?
-Whoa!

522
00:43:13.967 --> 00:43:16.635
Hey, magic make this go a lot faster!

523
00:43:23.435 --> 00:43:25.102
Let's go to work.

524
00:43:42.579 --> 00:43:45.164
-Good gracious!
-Oh, no!

525
00:43:46.208 --> 00:43:48.751
-I'm trying to sew.
-I'm splattered!

526
00:43:48.835 --> 00:43:51.420
-How awful!
-It's tragic!

527
00:43:51.505 --> 00:43:54.089
-I feel a bit pale.
-Watch out! That's my tail!

528
00:43:54.174 --> 00:43:56.509
I think we've had quite enough magic.

529
00:44:02.974 --> 00:44:04.892
-What a mess!
-It's a mess, all right.

530
00:44:04.976 --> 00:44:06.143
A big, stinky mess.

531
00:44:06.228 --> 00:44:08.354
-We've seen worse!
-Yeah.

532
00:44:08.438 --> 00:44:10.523
Remember when Anastasia fell in love?

533
00:44:10.607 --> 00:44:12.107
I sure do.

534
00:44:12.192 --> 00:44:15.444
Cinderella's stepsister?
That Anastasia?

535
00:44:15.529 --> 00:44:18.364
-Yeah!
-Now that's a messy story.

536
00:44:18.448 --> 00:44:21.200
No. It's a love story.

537
00:44:44.349 --> 00:44:45.975
Lucifer!

538
00:44:51.731 --> 00:44:53.732
Stop hogging the mirror!

539
00:44:55.861 --> 00:44:58.112
-That's mine!
-No! It's mine!

540
00:44:58.196 --> 00:45:01.115
-No! Mine!
-Hey! That's mine!

541
00:45:03.076 --> 00:45:05.244
Oh, you're right.

542
00:45:05.328 --> 00:45:08.873
-It is yours.
-You did that on purpose!

543
00:45:08.957 --> 00:45:10.583
-Did not!
-Did too!

544
00:45:10.667 --> 00:45:11.709
-Did not!
-Did too.

545
00:45:11.793 --> 00:45:15.838
Girls, stop all this bickering at once!

546
00:45:15.922 --> 00:45:19.758
Cinderella's ball is tomorrow night,
so pay attention!

547
00:45:20.385 --> 00:45:23.345
Every noble bachelor
in the kingdom will be there.

548
00:45:23.430 --> 00:45:28.642
If you want to find a husband, you have
to make the most of this opportunity.

549
00:45:28.727 --> 00:45:31.937
I won't let you fail me, again.

550
00:45:32.772 --> 00:45:34.732
-Yes, Mother.
-Yes, Mother.

551
00:45:34.816 --> 00:45:37.359
Drizella, pin back those curls.

552
00:45:37.444 --> 00:45:41.071
Anastasia, put more colour
in your cheeks!

553
00:45:41.156 --> 00:45:45.910
A perfect appearance is the only way
to attract a proper gentleman.

554
00:45:45.994 --> 00:45:49.872
We shall find you
men of wealth and nobility.

555
00:45:50.373 --> 00:45:52.750
-Maybe a count.
-Or a duke.

556
00:45:52.834 --> 00:45:54.752
Precisely.

557
00:45:54.836 --> 00:45:57.796
Come along now.
We need new gowns for the both of you.

558
00:45:58.340 --> 00:46:01.425
-With new shoes.
-And jewellery.

559
00:46:01.509 --> 00:46:04.970
The fancier the better. Lucifer, come.

560
00:46:07.390 --> 00:46:08.641
Lucifer!

561
00:46:21.655 --> 00:46:24.615
Morning, Cinderelly!
Why you dressed like that?

562
00:46:24.699 --> 00:46:27.952
I'm going to the market in disguise
so no one will recognise me.

563
00:46:28.036 --> 00:46:31.455
I want to surprise the Prince
with a garland of flowers.

564
00:46:31.539 --> 00:46:34.667
-Want to come along?
-Oh, yeah. Let's go!

565
00:46:34.751 --> 00:46:36.251
Gus-Gus come along.

566
00:47:01.194 --> 00:47:02.987
Remember the tradition.

567
00:47:04.114 --> 00:47:08.117
Give these to each other at the ball,
and you'll always be together.

568
00:47:09.703 --> 00:47:12.454
Don't you need
a garland of roses for the ball?

569
00:47:16.292 --> 00:47:18.460
Guaranteed to win you his heart.

570
00:47:18.545 --> 00:47:20.963
Anastasia, what are you doing?

571
00:47:21.047 --> 00:47:23.716
Nothing. Coming.

572
00:48:01.921 --> 00:48:05.340
Everything smells so good.

573
00:48:05.425 --> 00:48:08.886
Would you like one?
Be careful. They're hot.

574
00:48:10.597 --> 00:48:13.682
Anastasia, I think not.

575
00:48:13.767 --> 00:48:18.228
Everything in this shop is inferior.

576
00:48:19.564 --> 00:48:21.774
You can build a house
out of these bricks.

577
00:48:21.858 --> 00:48:23.901
Come along, Anastasia.

578
00:48:27.655 --> 00:48:32.034
You're not to say a word
to that shopkeeper.

579
00:48:32.118 --> 00:48:34.912
-I forbid it!
-Yes, Mother.

580
00:48:37.207 --> 00:48:38.540
He's got that look,

581
00:48:40.001 --> 00:48:42.044
and I know that look.

582
00:48:42.128 --> 00:48:43.128
Seasick?

583
00:48:45.548 --> 00:48:49.426
Oh, very funny. I think they're in love.

584
00:48:49.511 --> 00:48:53.222
Anastasia's in love?
That's crazy, Cinderelly!

585
00:48:53.306 --> 00:48:56.642
Come on, you two.
Anyone can fall in love.

586
00:48:56.976 --> 00:48:59.311
Anyone but Anastasia.

587
00:48:59.979 --> 00:49:04.149
-Maybe she just needs some help.
-Yeah, lots of help.

588
00:49:04.234 --> 00:49:07.319
Well, I had lots of help, too, remember?

589
00:49:08.738 --> 00:49:12.407
We have to figure out
how to get them together again.

590
00:49:12.492 --> 00:49:17.830
I know! We'll lure them into the square,
and here's how we'll do it.

591
00:49:17.914 --> 00:49:19.248
The birds will get her hat.

592
00:49:19.332 --> 00:49:21.750
Get the baker's attention.
Bring Anastasia here.

593
00:49:21.835 --> 00:49:24.920
Get the baker outside.
They'll meet in front of the shop.

594
00:49:26.506 --> 00:49:29.508
That's right, Gus.
They'll never know what hit them.

595
00:49:37.642 --> 00:49:40.227
-Hey.
-Okay, fellas...

596
00:49:40.311 --> 00:49:43.063
Get his attention, and remember,
keep it simple.

597
00:50:09.549 --> 00:50:11.675
Mice in my baguettes!

598
00:50:20.435 --> 00:50:21.476
Lucifey!

599
00:50:29.027 --> 00:50:33.113
Come back here!
Filthy creatures!

600
00:50:53.134 --> 00:50:54.426
Are you okay?

601
00:50:55.887 --> 00:50:58.347
Oh, no!

602
00:51:19.118 --> 00:51:20.452
Anastasia?

603
00:51:22.288 --> 00:51:25.707
What are you doing here
dressed like that?

604
00:51:25.792 --> 00:51:28.168
You look like a laundry maid.

605
00:51:28.920 --> 00:51:31.505
I'm not the one with egg on my face.

606
00:51:36.427 --> 00:51:38.720
I saw you in the baker's shop.

607
00:51:39.639 --> 00:51:41.139
He must think I'm...

608
00:51:43.393 --> 00:51:47.604
He saw it was an accident.
Don't give up so fast.

609
00:51:47.689 --> 00:51:51.400
What would you know?
You're beautiful.

610
00:51:51.484 --> 00:51:53.777
It's always been easy for you.

611
00:51:53.861 --> 00:51:57.239
Easy? That's not how I remember it.

612
00:51:57.323 --> 00:52:00.951
Look, Anastasia, you just need
a little help, that's all.

613
00:52:01.035 --> 00:52:03.745
If I weren't so clumsy and plain...

614
00:52:03.830 --> 00:52:06.123
Listen, why don't you
come back to the castle?

615
00:52:06.791 --> 00:52:09.418
We'll clean you up
and then we'll get you two together.

616
00:52:10.211 --> 00:52:14.089
But Mother forbids it!
She thinks he's beneath me.

617
00:52:14.173 --> 00:52:17.592
And I think she's wrong.
The baker's terrific.

618
00:52:17.677 --> 00:52:19.344
And he cooks, too.

619
00:53:40.551 --> 00:53:43.845
Lucifey like Pom-Pom, yes?

620
00:53:43.930 --> 00:53:49.017
Mice can help if Lucifey promise
to stop chasing mice!

621
00:53:49.102 --> 00:53:50.143
Deal?

622
00:54:01.614 --> 00:54:04.699
-There. Good as new.
-Don't stop now!

623
00:54:04.784 --> 00:54:07.494
Mother says that looks
count for everything.

624
00:54:07.578 --> 00:54:10.705
Well, of course you want to
look your best,

625
00:54:10.790 --> 00:54:12.707
but that's not the most important thing.

626
00:54:12.792 --> 00:54:16.002
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
What I need is a whole new look.

627
00:54:17.338 --> 00:54:19.673
Make me Iook good
make me look swell

628
00:54:19.757 --> 00:54:21.758
Make me look fine

629
00:54:23.428 --> 00:54:25.804
We're pourin' it on, you just sit back

630
00:54:25.888 --> 00:54:29.099
'Cause, baby, you're mine

631
00:54:29.183 --> 00:54:32.352
You send me into a spin

632
00:54:32.437 --> 00:54:35.355
Make a spIash when you waIk in

633
00:54:35.440 --> 00:54:39.401
Those eyes so rare, the Iips, the hair

634
00:54:39.485 --> 00:54:41.528
You're a breath of fresh air

635
00:54:44.365 --> 00:54:46.450
irushing the fur, comb the hair out

636
00:54:46.534 --> 00:54:48.535
Trim up the toes

637
00:54:49.954 --> 00:54:51.955
Give me the dress and the shoes

638
00:54:52.039 --> 00:54:55.625
And the jeweIIery and cIothes

639
00:54:55.710 --> 00:54:58.628
You can judge your books
from how the cover looks

640
00:54:58.713 --> 00:55:02.090
Wear makeup by the ounce

641
00:55:02.175 --> 00:55:07.345
iut didn't they teII you
it's what's inside that counts?

642
00:55:08.055 --> 00:55:10.307
Make me a star, make me Iook great

643
00:55:10.391 --> 00:55:13.477
Make me Iook grand

644
00:55:13.561 --> 00:55:16.646
I've got styIe and grace
but it's a painted-up face

645
00:55:16.731 --> 00:55:19.316
Gets you a man

646
00:55:20.193 --> 00:55:22.444
Snip, cut, when we are through

647
00:55:22.528 --> 00:55:25.405
You're gonna Iook so good, it's true

648
00:55:25.490 --> 00:55:28.658
The fur, the bows, the chin, the nose

649
00:55:31.829 --> 00:55:37.292
Looks won't hide
it's what's inside that counts

650
00:55:37.376 --> 00:55:43.381
You wanna be a bride
it's what's inside that counts

651
00:55:43.925 --> 00:55:45.800
What about a necklace?

652
00:55:49.847 --> 00:55:51.848
-Lucifer!
-Stupid cat.

653
00:55:54.185 --> 00:55:58.647
Remember, you'll catch more flies
with honey than with vinegar.

654
00:55:58.731 --> 00:56:01.816
What does that mean?
Who'd want to catch flies?

655
00:56:01.901 --> 00:56:06.738
I mean the best way to impress
the baker is just to be nice to him.

656
00:56:06.822 --> 00:56:11.409
-How do I do that?
-You could start with a smile.

657
00:56:11.494 --> 00:56:13.828
Better get me a bigger necklace.

658
00:56:17.250 --> 00:56:18.500
Come on.

659
00:56:40.147 --> 00:56:43.525
-I make babies cry, too.
-Here.

660
00:56:47.446 --> 00:56:49.698
He'll never be able to resist.

661
00:56:49.782 --> 00:56:51.283
You think so?

662
00:56:52.368 --> 00:56:54.536
But what if Mother catches me?

663
00:56:54.620 --> 00:56:57.789
She told me never to speak
to the baker again!

664
00:56:57.873 --> 00:57:00.542
It's time to stop following
someone else's orders

665
00:57:00.626 --> 00:57:03.378
and start following your heart.

666
00:57:04.380 --> 00:57:06.881
It's late! I have to go!

667
00:57:06.966 --> 00:57:08.967
But what about the baker?

668
00:57:11.012 --> 00:57:13.638
I could walk you to his shop.

669
00:57:13.723 --> 00:57:16.933
Meet you in the market
at noon tomorrow?

670
00:57:17.018 --> 00:57:18.685
I can hardly wait!

671
00:58:31.592 --> 00:58:35.387
Mother, I have to run to town.
We're out of bread.

672
00:58:36.347 --> 00:58:37.389
Hey!

673
00:58:38.766 --> 00:58:40.392
Excuse me. Can I borrow this? Thanks!

674
00:59:18.264 --> 00:59:19.931
I'll wait for you by the apple cart.

675
00:59:27.606 --> 00:59:32.318
-Do you think she'll like them?
-They're beautiful! She'll love them!

676
00:59:58.429 --> 01:00:00.680
What? What happened?

677
01:00:04.143 --> 01:00:05.894
Anastasia!

678
01:01:30.980 --> 01:01:32.063
Run for it!

679
01:01:56.422 --> 01:01:58.298
The deal is off!

680
01:02:53.062 --> 01:02:55.813
Don't look at me! I look horrible!

681
01:02:56.565 --> 01:02:58.232
Wait! Please!

682
01:03:19.171 --> 01:03:20.838
Anastasia!

683
01:03:21.423 --> 01:03:24.467
How dare you defy me?

684
01:03:24.551 --> 01:03:27.011
You were forbidden
to speak to this man!

685
01:03:27.096 --> 01:03:30.765
Look at her! It's a disaster!

686
01:03:30.849 --> 01:03:33.851
We'll be the laughingstock
of the entire town.

687
01:03:34.728 --> 01:03:38.564
You've embarrassed yourself
quite enough with this foolishness.

688
01:03:40.025 --> 01:03:44.946
Dear child, you know I only have
your best interests at heart.

689
01:03:45.030 --> 01:03:47.782
You deserve better. Come along.

690
01:03:47.866 --> 01:03:50.660
No, Mother! You're wrong!

691
01:03:52.871 --> 01:03:55.623
-He's sweet.
-She's wonderful.

692
01:03:55.708 --> 01:04:00.545
He's romantic.
And we are going to the ball together.

693
01:04:09.096 --> 01:04:11.305
Drizella, come along.

694
01:04:16.395 --> 01:04:18.021
Drizella!

695
01:04:46.258 --> 01:04:49.594
Thank you!
I never dreamed I could be this happy.

696
01:04:49.678 --> 01:04:52.263
You see? Dreams do come true.

697
01:05:19.166 --> 01:05:20.958
Looks good!

698
01:05:25.672 --> 01:05:28.049
Needs something.

699
01:05:28.133 --> 01:05:30.051
Gus-Gus, where's your bow?

700
01:05:33.138 --> 01:05:34.514
Right here.

701
01:05:36.058 --> 01:05:38.392
-Ta-da!
-Perfect.

702
01:05:41.355 --> 01:05:44.982
-All finished!
-Are you ready to show Cinderella?

703
01:05:45.526 --> 01:05:48.069
Look! There she is.

704
01:05:48.153 --> 01:05:50.071
Let's go!

705
01:05:51.573 --> 01:05:53.407
Salagadoola mechicka boola

706
01:05:53.492 --> 01:05:54.951
iibbidi-bobbidi-boo

707
01:05:55.035 --> 01:05:57.161
Put 'em together
and what have you got?

708
01:05:57.246 --> 01:05:59.247
iibbidi-bobbidi-boo

709
01:05:59.331 --> 01:06:02.750
Salagadoola mechicka boola
iibbidi-bobbidi-boo

710
01:06:02.835 --> 01:06:06.587
It'II do magic, beIieve it or not
iibbidi-bobbidi-boo

711
01:06:06.672 --> 01:06:10.424
Now saIagadooIa-mee
and mechicka boola-roo

712
01:06:10.509 --> 01:06:14.595
iut the thingamabob that does the job
is bibbidi-bobbidi-boo

713
01:06:17.516 --> 01:06:20.434
-Cinderelly!
-Cinderelly!

714
01:06:20.519 --> 01:06:22.895
Look what we made!

715
01:06:24.857 --> 01:06:26.858
Look out!

716
01:06:30.863 --> 01:06:34.824
-What's this?
-It's a book. We made it!

717
01:06:34.908 --> 01:06:39.412
-Do ya like it?
-I love it! What's it about?

718
01:06:39.496 --> 01:06:42.790
-It's about all of us.
-How wonderful!

719
01:06:42.875 --> 01:06:46.586
I don't suppose you'd want
to read this together, would you?

720
01:06:46.670 --> 01:06:49.505
-All right!
-Oh, boy!

721
01:06:49.590 --> 01:06:51.215
Oh, boy! Oh, boy!

722
01:06:52.676 --> 01:06:54.802
Oh, look!

723
01:06:54.887 --> 01:06:59.140
We're all in here.
And these are our stories.

724
01:06:59.224 --> 01:07:02.310
"Once upon a time
there was a big castle,

725
01:07:02.394 --> 01:07:05.229
"and in this castle lived
a Prince and a Princess..."
